  "source_before": "834fafafcbf49bf4b1b29577f8e3c35d9c11b78b",
  "architecture": [
    "Strict boolean direction_wedges is shared by Rust configuration and scene builders, serialized descriptions, command parser/printer, Python keyword/stub and WASM contract. No binding duplicates geometry semantics.",
    "Each selected CA/C4-prime guide owns one flat triangle including terminal guides. Its width and length are half the authored ribbon width. Full-parent ordered traces orient isolated selections without rendering their neighbors.",
    "Isolated source residues use N/CA/C or C5-prime/C4-prime/C3-prime backbone anchors. Missing or degenerate directions return CartoonError; failed generation clears emitted output rather than uploading a partial mesh.",
    "The existing 32-byte deformation recipe gains an atom-anchor mode in its reserved lane. Shared beauty, OIT, shadow and picking shaders read the same resident source coordinates; no coordinate column is copied and no new GPU layout, pass or per-frame upload is introduced.",
    "Conservative glyph bounds use the shared profile resolver and narrow cached width/aspect/kind keys; camera-only updates reuse cached bounds.",
    "The gallery generator now reproduces all 71 committed fixture definitions, including eight earlier cartoon cases and the corrected uniform Mol* Tube reference."
  ],
  "complexity": "Cold direction generation is O(source guides + adaptive samples), with pooled O(guides + samples) working storage and three vertices/indices per selected guide. Static camera rendering does not regenerate glyphs.",
